\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Thy Kingdom come, O God;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   Thy rule, O Christ, begin;
\par  Break with Thine iron rod
\par The tyrannies of sin.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Where is Thy reign of peace
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  And purity of love?
\par  When shall all hatred cease,
\par   As in the realms above?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  When comes the promised time
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   That war shall be no more,
\par   And lust, oppression, crime,
\par   Shall flee Thy face before?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. We pray Thee, Lord, arise,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 And come in Thy great might;
\par Revive our longing eyes,
\par Which languish for Thy sight.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Men scorn Thy sacred Name,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 And wolves devour Thy fold;
\par By many deeds of shame
\par We learn that love grows cold.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  O'er heathen lands afar
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Thick darkness broodeth yet;
\par Arise, O Morning Star,
\par \pard        Arise, and never set.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

